title: Describe heralds
pid: 639e7ea2-4e90-4814-be39-472569c2e68d
body: |2-
    - Request: ((request . "describe heralds") (metadata . "(skg ...)")
      [(folder-change . "processed" | "unprocessed")])
    - Response: LP response-type "describe-heralds" with
      =((lines "SENTENCE" ...))=, or =((error "MESSAGE"))= when the
      metadata does not read.
    - The metadata is one headline's, as the client's buffer holds it.
      A client adds the atom =pendingDetachment= when the headline is a
      pending detachment, and on a folder of the diff view whose
      members' relationships changed sends =folder-change=, whether
      every such change is processed: what it draws itself ("Herald
      rules" above; 'docs/heralds.org', "What the server serves, and
      what the clients add"). The server reads nothing else but its
      config, for skgrepo labels and ownership.
    - The sentences ('server/herald_descriptions.rs'): for a folder,
      first what it holds and how its members relate to the note above
      it; then one per herald, with the headline's own counts, ancestor
      letters and skgrepos read out, ordered by the herald's style, the
      styles asking more attention first. A sentence is keyed on the
      path in the metadata of the element that makes its herald appear;
      a path the rule table renders that no sentence covers reads "No
      description yet for PATH.", and the unit test
      =every_herald_the_rule_table_renders_has_a_sentence= requires
      that there be none (=every_folder_has_a_sentence_beginning_with_its_label=
      does the same for the folders). 'skg-describe-at-point' (=C-c v
      ?=), ':SkgDescribeAtPoint' and skg-for-ai's 'describe' show them.
